{"description":"Agents consuming eka-mcp repeatedly hit tool failures whose results carry only a count-only summary, forcing fallback to the CLI for diagnosis. Observed live twice in one session (2026-08-26): publishing a plan draft was refused with 'failed CKO-level validation with 1 blocking error(s)' and NO rule detail (the actual finding - R6 missing dimension - surfaced only after falling back to the CLI); publishing a bug draft repeated the pattern (R9 missing impact section). Each fallback costs a round trip and trains agents to route around the sanctioned API surface.\n\nRevision 2: per owner decision this item is tracked in EKA only - the conditional GitHub-issue acceptance criterion from v1 is removed; no external issue exists or will be filed for this item.\n\nRoot cause verified in source - the data is structured end-to-end and discarded at ONE point:\n- Core produces structured errors: *runtime.PublishError{Target, Report} carries the full conformance.Report (rule R0-R12, severity, message per finding); same pattern for relate validation errors. Error() renders only the count summary; the Report field is exported and reachable via errors.As.\n- The CLI unwraps (errors.As) and prints the full report - it does NOT re-run validation.\n- The MCP boundary flattens: tool failures are wrapped into isError:true results whose text is SanitizeError(err) - first line only plus path redaction. Zero errors.As usage exists anywhere in the MCP server, so the carried Report is silently dropped on every refusal.\n- Secondary fidelity loss: transition refusals cross MCP as Reason+Hint only; their Warning and Confirmation fields are dropped, so an agent is never told a membership-gate refusal can be retried with confirmed:true even though the capability layer supports it.\n\nProtocol facts (verified): the server negotiates the 2024-11-05 baseline (echoing the client's announced version); tool results are hand-built maps {content:[{type:text}], isError}; BOTH multi-line text and multiple text content blocks are spec-valid on that baseline; execution failures intentionally ride result.isError rather than JSON-RPC error codes, so enriching the payload touches no error-code semantics; structuredContent (a newer-spec feature) is unnecessary and risky for strict older clients.\n\nFix direction (ranked): (a) ADOPT - unwrap structured errors at the capability/MCP boundary via errors.As; serialize the full report inline using the already-established conformance-report shape; keep the sanitized first line as a stable headline; apply path redaction to finding text; surface transition Warning/Confirmation affordances. Tens of lines, no core change, no protocol risk. (b) REJECT - re-running validation on refusal: double cost, TOCTOU drift risk, bespoke handling per refusal class. (c) STOPGAP ONLY - documenting the companion validate tool for self-service diagnosis: agents demonstrably fall back to the CLI instead (twice in one session), and it leaves transition confirmation affordances invisible.","acceptanceCriteria":"- Publish/relate/note-resolve refusals over MCP embed the FULL CKO validation report (per-finding rule id, severity, message; warnings included) - not just the blocking-error count.\n- The sanitized headline line stays byte-stable (existing client matching and hardening tests keep passing); finding text passes the same path-redaction policy as the headline.\n- Transition refusal results surface the warning and the confirmation affordance ('retry with confirmed:true') whenever the refusal carries a confirmation flag - today that information is silently dropped.\n- The report is serialized in the established eka-conformance-report-v1 shape, delivered as a second text content block or appended multi-line text (both valid on the server's baseline protocol version; no structuredContent dependency).\n- Hardening tests extended: multi-line fidelity at the boundary, no path/store leakage inside findings, headline stability.\n- Troubleshooting skill docs updated to state that authoring refusals now embed the report inline (no CLI fallback needed for diagnosis).\n- Tracking decision (owner, 2026-08-26): this item is tracked in EKA knowledge ONLY - no GitHub issue is filed for it; completion evidence lives in this line's history and its container."}